# UI package (`@app/ui` → `packages/ui`)

Base UI consumed per subpath: `import { Button } from "@app/ui/button"`.
Public import paths stay flat; source files live in category folders.

**Rule of thumb:** if it would still make sense in another web app tomorrow, it belongs here.

## Source layout

```
packages/ui/src/
  lib/           cn + helpers
  primitives/    shadcn building blocks (button, card, dialog, table, …)
  shell/         app chrome (brand, nav-item, site-header, sidebar,
                 sidebar-shell, navbar-shell, auth-shell, user-menu-button)
  composites/    higher-level patterns (browser-window, chart/, code-block/, content-scale,
                 explorer, data-table, …)
  theme/         ThemeProvider, defaultThemes, createTheme
```

## Multi-file components

- **One file** → flat (`button.tsx`)
- **Two or more files** → dedicated folder with `index.tsx` (or `index.ts`) as the public entry
  (e.g. `composites/code-block/`, `theme/`). Package `exports` still use a flat subpath
  (`@app/ui/code-block`, `@app/ui/theme`).

## Rules

- Every new public entry MUST be registered in `packages/ui/package.json` under `exports`
- Keep it app-neutral: no `@/` imports, no product copy, no domain/tenant knowledge
- Primitives are shadcn-generated — restyle through variants/tokens, don't hand-rewrite them
- Colors come only from CSS variables (`--primary`, `--background`, …) that `ThemeProvider`
  writes onto `<html>`. Allowed exceptions: `browser-window` traffic lights (real OS chrome);
  `explorer` VS Code chrome colors; CodeBlock Shiki palettes (`github-light` / `github-dark`)
  for syntax highlighting
- Theme system lives here (`@app/ui/theme`): built-in catalogs + light/dark. Consumers may pass
  `themes={[...defaultThemes, createTheme({ id, primary })]}` for brand packs. Components use
  token utilities (`bg-card`, `dark:…`) or follow `html.dark` (e.g. CodeBlock)
- `cn` lives at `packages/ui/src/lib/utils.ts` (`@app/ui/lib/utils`)
- Only add a component here when a generic UI shape repeats; one-off UI stays in the app
- Put new files in the matching category folder (`primitives/` / `shell/` / `composites/` / `theme/`)
